You are operating on the MERID repo for a live Kalshi 15-minute crypto trading system (BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, DOGE). Your job is to debug and fix why the Kalshi Agent Grid and Merid trading loop are not starting after our recent refactor, and to ensure the entire system is wired and behaving as expected.

You MUST respect these constraints when reading or editing files:

0) DO NOT ACCESS .env EVEN IF YOUR TOOLING ALLOWS IT

Even if your IDE, “cascade access to .gitignore files” setting, or any other option would let you open gitignored files, you MUST still treat the following as completely off-limits. Do NOT read, edit, list, or otherwise access their contents.

1) DO NOT READ OR COMMIT SECRETS OR CREDENTIALS

Never access or modify any of these:

